OSI Model - 
	It divides network communication into 7 layers, from physical signals to application protocols. Its main purpose is to give engineers a common way to understand and troubleshoot network problems.
	
| Layer | Name         | Main Job                                       | Examples                                    |
| ----- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| **7** | Application  | Application-level communication                | HTTP, DNS, SMTP, SSH, gRPC                  |
| **6** | Presentation | Data format, encoding, compression, encryption | JSON, Protobuf, UTF-8, TLS, gzip            |
| **5** | Session      | Manage communication sessions                  | WebSocket, gRPC streams, session resumption |
| **4** | Transport    | Process-to-process delivery                    | TCP, UDP, QUIC                              |
| **3** | Network      | Routing between networks                       | IP, ICMP, BGP, OSPF                         |
| **2** | Data Link    | Local network/frame delivery                   | Ethernet, WiFi, MAC, VLAN                   |
| **1** | Physical     | Transfer raw bits/signals                      | Cables, fiber, radio                        |


Layer 1 - Physical - Move raw bits through Ethernet cable, Fiber, wifi. Problems - bad cable, slow wifi.

Layer 2 - Data Link - Handles communication on the local network , concepts - MAC addresses, Frames, Switches, data unit - frame.

Layer 3 - Network - Move packets between different networks - concepts - ip addresses, routers, routing tables, ipv4/ipv6, icmp , data unit - packet.

Layer 4 - Transport - provides process to process communication - concepts - ports, tcp, udp, flow control, congestion control. data units - tcp - segment , udp - datagram.

Layer 5 - Session - Deals with starting, maintaining, resuming and closing sessions. concepts - Webhooks, Connection Pooling, TLS session resumption.

Layer 6 - Presentation - Deals with how data is represented. includes - serialization, encoding, compression, Encryption.

Layer 7 - Application - where actual application protocol operates - e.g - http/https, dns, ssh, smtp, gRPC

Encapsulation -
	when sending data, each layer adds it own information.
	
tcp/ip has four layers - Physical (1+2) , Internet (3), Transport (4), Application (5+6+7).

